#: ../../../core/migration.rst:18
msgid "Migrating from 5.x to 6.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:20
msgid ""
"Guidance on how to upgrade from :ref:`piocore` v5.x to v6.x with emphasis on "
"major changes, what is new, and what has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:24
msgid ""
"PlatformIO Core 6.0 is **FULLY BACKWARD COMPATIBLE*** with PlatformIO 5.0 "
"projects. It means, there are no breaking changes or required migration "
"steps. Project compatibility between major PlatformIO Core releases is our "
"main task and part of PlatformIO's decentralized architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:29
msgid ""
"We highly recommend using the latest PlatformIO Core. See :ref:`cmd_upgrade` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:32
msgid ""
"``*`` see a note regarding :ref:`unit_testing` and the grouped test suites "
"in the migration steps below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:35
msgid ""
"Please read :ref:`PlatformIO 6.0 Release Notes <release_notes_6>` before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:38
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:41
msgid "Migration Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:43
msgid ""
"|CORE_6_0| received a lot of new features and updates to improve the lives "
"of everyday engineers. To benefit from its improvements, we recommend taking "
"into account the following steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:47
msgid ""
"Replace deprecated :ref:`cmd_lib`, :ref:`cmd_platform`, and :ref:"
"`cmd_update` commands with the unified :ref:`cmd_pkg`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:49
msgid ""
"Avoid using global libraries previously installed using the :option:`pio lib "
"--global` command. Ensure that the :ref:`projectconf_pio_globallib_dir` "
"folder is empty. Please use a declarative approach for the safety-critical "
"embedded development and declare project dependencies using the :ref:"
"`projectconf_lib_deps` option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:53
msgid ""
"Ensure that project dependencies are declared using the :ref:"
"`projectconf_env_platform`, :ref:`projectconf_env_platform_packages`, and :"
"ref:`projectconf_lib_deps` options in :ref:`projectconf`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:57
msgid "meet the updated :ref:`cmd_pkg_install_specifications`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:58
msgid ""
"use recommended Semantic :ref:`cmd_pkg_install_requirements` (check |"
"PIOREGISTRY| for the available package versions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:61
msgid "**Bad practice** (not recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:83
msgid "**Good practice** (highly recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:108
msgid ""
"If you use a custom testing transport via the \"test_transport\" option in :"
"ref:`projectconf`, please align your codebase with :ref:"
"`unit_testing_frameworks_unity_custom_config`. The \"test_transport\" option "
"has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:113
msgid ""
"There is a known bug in PlatformIO Core 5.0 when Unit Testing didn't handle "
"correctly grouped test suites. Please ensure that a test suite folder that "
"contains test source files is prefixed with ``test_``. See :ref:"
"`unit_testing_test_hierarchy` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:119
msgid "What is new"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:121
msgid ""
"In this section, we are going to highlight the most important changes and "
"features introduced in |CORE_6_0|. Please visit :ref:`PlatformIO 6.0 Release "
"Notes <release_notes_6>` for more detailed information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:126
msgid "Package Management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:128
msgid ""
"|CORE_6_0| brings a powerful solution to manage different :ref:"
"`cmd_pkg_install_types` using the unified :ref:`cmd_pkg`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:131
msgid ""
":ref:`cmd_pkg_install` - install the project dependencies or custom packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:132
msgid ":ref:`cmd_pkg_list` - list installed packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:133
msgid ":ref:`cmd_pkg_outdated` - check for project outdated packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:134
msgid ":ref:`cmd_pkg_search` - search for packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:135
msgid ":ref:`cmd_pkg_show` - show package information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:136
msgid ""
":ref:`cmd_pkg_uninstall` uninstall the project dependencies or custom "
"packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:137
msgid ""
":ref:`cmd_pkg_update` - update the project dependencies or custom packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:139
msgid ""
"There are no more global packages that could lead to potential issues. The "
"new package management solution allows you to use a modern declarative "
"approach for safety-critical embedded development. Using the Semantic :ref:"
"`cmd_pkg_install_requirements` guarantees the full project reproducibility "
"on any supported host machine for decades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:144
msgid ""
"The new :ref:`cmd_pkg` operates in accordance with the active (working) "
"project. The :ref:`cmd_pkg_install` command will install all required "
"project dependencies. The :ref:`cmd_pkg_list` command allows listing not "
"only dependent libraries but also development platforms and their packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:149
msgid ""
"The notable addition is the :ref:`cmd_pkg_outdated` command. It allows you "
"to check for outdated project packages and list version information for all "
"dependencies. There are three color legends to help you easily identify "
"which updates are backward-incompatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:155
msgid "Run package command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:157
msgid ""
"|PIOREGISTRY| contains a rich set of popular toolchains and other useful "
"tools. The :ref:`cmd_pkg_exec` command allows you to run an arbitrary "
"command from the specified package. If you specify package requirements "
"using the :option:`pio pkg exec --package` option, PlatformIO will ensure "
"that the package is installed before running any command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:162
msgid ""
"Practical use cases include running debugging servers, uploaders or special "
"tools from a toolchain. A few examples of how to leverage the new :ref:"
"`cmd_pkg_exec` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:178
msgid "Virtual symbolic links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:180
msgid ""
"The most requested feature from the library maintainers was the ability to "
"link the existing package with the project without hard copying "
"(duplicating). As a workaround, developers used a Unix-native symlink "
"solution and hence it was not possible to declare a symlinked dependency in "
"the :ref:`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:185
msgid ""
"The :ref:`piocore` 6.0 introduces cross-platform virtual symbolic links "
"without any dependencies on the host OS. PlatformIO ``symlink://`` resources "
"do not require any specific OS permissions. They are portable between "
"different host machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:190
msgid "See :ref:`cmd_pkg_install_specifications` for \"Local Folder\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:193
msgid "Unit Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:195
msgid ""
"It's been `six years <https://github.com/platformio/platformio-core/commit/"
"bb22a1297bc2e4c3131530f15a2b4b3914836560>`_ since we added support for unit "
"testing, and Unity was the only available testing framework. We didn't "
"expect that the PlatformIO :ref:`unit_testing` solution will gain broad "
"popularity, especially when it comes to using it on native (host) machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:200
msgid ""
"So, the time has come to refresh our view on PlatformIO Unit Testing with "
"taking into account `your feedback and feature requests <https://github.com/"
"platformio/platformio-core/issues?"
"q=is%3Aissue+label%3A%22unit+testing%22+is%3Aclosed+milestone%3A6.0>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:204
msgid "Test-driven development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:206
msgid ""
"The PlatformIO Core 6.0 introduces an absolutely a new workflow for `test-"
"driven development <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test-driven_development>`_ "
"in the embedded systems industry. Thanks to the rich set of supported :ref:"
"`unit_testing_frameworks` and the ability to organize tests in groups using "
"the :ref:`unit_testing_test_hierarchy`, you can create hybrid projects and "
"benefit from multiple testing frameworks depending on the project "
"requirements simultaneously. See a simple example of the hybrid "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:231
msgid ""
"Use more advanced C++ testing frameworks with Mocking support such as :ref:"
"`unit_testing_frameworks_googletest` in pair with the :ref:`platform_native` "
"development platform to run desktop tests on the host machine and a "
"lightweight framework, such as :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks_unity`, for "
"running tests on the target embedded device with constrained resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:238
msgid "Hardware-less development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:240
msgid ""
"It's hard to imagine today a next-gen project development workflow that does "
"not benefit from :ref:`ci` systems. PlatformIO already provides multiple "
"solutions to improve code quality including :ref:`check`. In addition to the "
"testing frameworks that allow you to mock objects and simulate the behavior "
"of real objects, the PlatformIO Core 6.0 adds support for the :ref:"
"`unit_testing_simulators`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:247
msgid ""
"The combination of simulation tools and testing frameworks allow you to "
"simulate hardware systems and run unit tests in virtual environments. "
"Simulators can significantly accelerate project development, especially when "
"used in pair with :ref:`ci`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:252
msgid ""
"Integration of any simulator tool to the PlatformIO :ref:`unit_testing` is "
"very simple and does not require any extra software or code writing. Please "
"take a look at the example below how easy it is to integrate the :ref:"
"`unit_testing_simulators_renode` simulation framework:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:275
msgid "What is changed or removed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:278
msgid "Dropped automatic updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:280
msgid ""
"Thanks to your feedback, we finally removed automatic updates of global "
"libraries and development platforms. Please use :ref:`cmd_pkg_outdated` to "
"check for outdated project packages and list version information for all "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/migration.rst:284
msgid ""
"The :ref:`cmd_pkg_update` is intended to update the project dependencies, "
"custom packages from the |PIOREGISTRY|, or external sources."
msgstr ""

